ISSUE TITLE: Max size of attribute text content
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
There is a limitation with MISP attributes as the text type can contain maximum of 65535 characters, they suggest usage of attachments instead.

This does not seem to be a big use case for the items in Taranis - but currently the attribute with an overflow is just dropped. Instead, the text length should be adjusted to always make it to MISP at least partially.

It could finish with: `The rest of the content was truncated...`

Another solution would be to use attachments but this could become very complex to handle very quickly.

ISSUE LABELS: bug, collaboration
DIFFICULTY: this is a HARD, cross-cutting issue. Think before patching: identify every caller and every test that touches this behaviour, keep edge cases consistent, and do not paper over the root cause with a local special-case.

